  sentences:
  - A dragon likes us! Do you like him my Arachnee?
  - ... ...
  - I don't think you can eat him my Arachnee.
  - Dragons only allow themselves to be eaten when they are fallen in battle.
  - ... ...?
  - I can't fight you, Spider. It would make my Princess sad.
  - Ooooh he's so romantic. But it would make Arachnee happy to eat dragon meat.
    What to do...
  - 'I shall fight in this tournament to the death my Princess. If I win, I''ll marry
    you, if I lose your spider may eat me in the soldier''s stead. '
  - So sweet. Yes. Let's do that. I hope you win. I also hope you don't. What a delightful
    dilemma!
  - ...Alright. Let the tournament begin.
